From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ufs: qcom: read clock frequencies from the OPP table

The controller operating-points-v2 property references the table.
required-opps references individual power-domain OPPs, not that table.
Using it silently falls back to 150 MHz, which is not an SM8650 UniPro
OPP. This local fix keeps controller cycle counts and the clock aligned.
---
--- a/drivers/ufs/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -316,7 +316,7 @@
 		goto fallback;
 
 	/* Try parsing the opps */
-	if (!ofnode_parse_phandle_with_args(node, "required-opps",
+	if (!ofnode_parse_phandle_with_args(node, "operating-points-v2",
 					    NULL, 0, 0, &opp_table) &&
 	    ofnode_device_is_compatible(opp_table.node, "operating-points-v2")) {
 		ofnode opp_node;
